      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T19:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There could be a potential Inefficiency in elan_image_read: Inside the for loop within elan_image_read, `tx_buf` is repeatedly zeroed and the first byte is set:\n\n```\nfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c ELAN_DMA_LOOP; i++) {\n    memset(tx_buf, 0, ELAN_SPI_TX_BUF_SIZE);\n    tx_buf[0] \u003d START_READ_IMAGE;\n    // ... spi transaction ...\n}\n```\n\nSince START_READ_IMAGE is a constant and the rest of `tx_buf` seems unused for the transmit part of this specific SPI transaction, initializing `tx_buf` before the loop would be more efficient.\n\nSuggestion: Move the `memset` and `tx_buf[0]` assignment outside and before the for loop.\n\n\n```\n// In elan_image_read\nmemset(tx_buf, 0, ELAN_SPI_TX_BUF_SIZE);\ntx_buf[0] \u003d START_READ_IMAGE;\nfor (i \u003d 0; i \u003c ELAN_DMA_LOOP; i++) {\n    // No need to reset tx_buf here\n    ret \u003d elan_spi_transaction_duplex(tx_buf, ELAN_SPI_TX_BUF_SIZE,\n                                      rx_buf, ELAN_SPI_RX_BUF_SIZE);\n    // ... rest of the loop ...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
